{"title":"Career roadmap · Museum Curator (Junior)","role":"Museum Curator (Junior)","summary":"A Junior Museum Curator supports the research, documentation, preservation, interpretation and exhibition of museum collections. The role can involve collection management, object research, cataloguing, exhibition development, provenance research, public education and digital museum projects.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Museology / Heritage Management"},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Strong direct alignment"}],"intro":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"A relevant BA can provide entry-level exposure, but curatorial roles at major museums frequently favour postgraduate qualifications in Museology, History, Archaeology, Art History, Heritage Studies or a related discipline."}]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Museology/Heritage Management","Museum Internship","Collections/Curatorial Assistant","Junior Curator","Assistant Curator","Curator","Senior Curator","Head of Curatorial/Collections","Museum Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build museum studies, heritage, art/history knowledge, collection documentation and exhibition skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in collections, exhibitions, archaeology, art history, cultural heritage or digital museums."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead exhibitions, collections or major research projects and develop institutional expertise."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Curator, Collections Head, Exhibition Director, Museum Programme Head or Museum Director."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"row